;; Controls of the lists of code ids of calls of known arity, as the test
;; tool gives them to the model (../../tools/flsemantics.ml, "The code ids
;; that a call of known arity lists"; decision D59 of
;; middle_end/flambda2/rocq/DECISIONS.md). The tool extends the compiler's
;; list under "newer version of", as far as the metadata of code that it
;; has and the scope of the call allow; and where a run is undefined it
;; looks at the state that has no step, to see whether the list alone
;; makes it undefined, with code that the compiler's reading of the list
;; may allow, in which case it does not check the unit.
;;
;; lists.expected is what ../../tools/flknownaritylists.exe prints: the
;; extension, and that test of a state, computed on terms of the model that
;; are made in that program, one for each case that the compiler makes
;; rarely or never (a chain through code declared deleted, a missing link,
;; a cycle, a call in the code of the prefix, the empty list, a version out
;; of scope, a run that stops at a call for its list alone or for something
;; else). `dune promote` updates it. Two units from OCaml are in
;; ../ocaml/pairs/ (known_arity_lists_*.ml), which has the rules that
;; compile a source with its own flags.

(rule
 (with-stdout-to
  lists.output
  (run ../../tools/flknownaritylists.exe)))

(rule
 (alias runtest)
 (action
  (diff lists.expected lists.output)))
